inense), tomato paste, fresh tomatoes, fermented locust bean (Parkia biglobosa), dry beans, peanut butter, fermented tamarind seed pods (Tamarindus indica); with the teaspoon 'yokhos' (dried oysters) and the larger, lighter-color 'touffa' dried whelk. Not shown including meat (as available), peanut oil (any other cooking oil as available) or salt to taste. The quantities shown were used in their entirety together for one recipe that fed 12 people.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Piki-photow&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Piki-photow (page does not exist)\">T.K. Naliaka</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"40233605":{"pageid":40233605,"ns":6,"title":"File:Deukhine - sauce with peanut butter and tamarind - cured, fermented ingredients.jpg","index":6,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":270665,"width":872,"height":752,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Deukhine_-_sauce_with_peanut_butter_and_tamarind_-_cured%2C_fermented_ingredients.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":552,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Deukhine_-_sauce_with_peanut_butter_and_tamarind_-_cured%2C_fermented_ingredients.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":552},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Deukhine_-_sauce_with_peanut_butter_and_tamarind_-_cured%2C_fermented_ingredients.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deukhine_-_sauce_with_peanut_butter_and_tamarind_-_cured,_fermented_ingredients.jpg","d